    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0174" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European Advisory Commission/58a:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-21T17:00:00-04:00">January 21, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>517. British Embassy informs us that based upon discussions at Moscow and Tehran,
                    British Government desires to propose that the European Advisory Commission set
                    up a special body to study question <pb facs="0175" n="163" xml:id="pg163"/> of
                    dismemberment of Germany. You are authorized to accept the subject of
                    dismemberment for discussion in the European Advisory Commission in any form the
                    Commissioners may decide.</p>
                <p>We consider that this subject is already before the Commission under penultimate
                    paragraph, Section B, of U. S. paper on treatment of Germany, referred to the
                    Commission by the Moscow Conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
